lesson: 90
title: Multiplying and dividing together
stars: 2
explain: Many problems need both: first multiply to find the whole, then divide to share it.
explain: 4 packs of 6 cards make 4 × 6 = 24 cards; shared among 3 friends that is 24 ÷ 3 = 8 cards each.
explain: Read carefully what is asked, and leave out numbers the question does not need.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing g=2..9 k=2..10 p=2..8 x=5..12
need: (g * k) % p == 0
answer: g * k / p
exercise: {a} buys {g} packs of {t}. Each pack has {k} {t}. {a.He} shares them equally among {p} friends. How many {t} does each friend get?
exercise: There are {g} boxes with {k} {t} in each. All the {t} are put into {p} equal piles. How many {t} are in each pile?
exercise: {a} gets {k} {t} a day for {g} days, then puts them equally into {p} baskets. How many {t} are in each basket?
exercise: {g} rows of {k} chairs are moved into {p} rooms, the same number in each room. How many chairs go into each room?
exercise: {a} and {b} have {g} bags of {k} {t}. They pack the {t} into {p} equal boxes. How many {t} are in each box?
test: How many {t} does each of {p} children get when {g} bags of {k} {t} are shared fairly between them?
test: {a} is {x} years old. {a.He} has {g} sheets with {k} stamps on each sheet and gives all the stamps equally to {p} cousins. How many stamps does each cousin get?
test: The {p} teams share equally the {t} from {g} crates, {k} {t} per crate. How many {t} does one team get?
test: {b} bakes {g} trays of {k} rolls and gives the same number of rolls to each of {p} neighbours, giving all the rolls away. How many rolls does each neighbour get?
exercise: {a} has {g} bags of {t} with {k} {t} per bag. {a.He} splits all of them equally among {p} friends. How many {t} does each friend get?
exercise: How many {t} does each of {p} children get if {g} packs of {k} {t} are shared out fairly?
exercise: There are {g} trays with {k} {t} on every tray. The {t} are put into {p} equal heaps. How many {t} go in each heap?
exercise: {g} packs, {k} {t} in each, shared equally by {p} kids. How many {t} does each kid get?
exercise: {a} collects {k} {t} each day for {g} days. Then {a.he} divides them evenly into {p} boxes. How many {t} go into each box?
exercise: A teacher in Texas has {g} boxes of {k} crayons. She gives the same number of crayons to each of {p} tables, using them all. How many crayons does each table get?
exercise: {a} and {b} buy {g} packets of {k} {t} apiece and share them evenly among {p} classmates. How many {t} does every classmate get?
exercise: {g} shelves hold {k} books each. The books are packed into {p} boxes with the same number in every box. How many books are in one box?
test: Each of {p} groups gets an equal share of {g} crates holding {k} {t} each. How many {t} does a group get?
test: In a school in Wales, {g} classes each make {k} paper stars. All the stars are hung equally on {p} trees. How many stars hang on each tree?
test: {a} is {x}. {a.He} picks {k} apples from each of {g} trees and packs them evenly into {p} baskets. How many apples go in one basket?
test: If {g} cartons of {k} {t} are divided equally between {p} teams, what is one team's share?
test: {p} children in Brisbane share {g} bags of {k} {t} so that each child gets as many as the others. How many {t} is that per child?
test: A farmer in Iowa fills {g} crates with {k} eggs apiece and then repacks every egg into {p} equal boxes. How many eggs are in each box?
exercise: {g} packs {k} {t} each, split between {p} of us. how many each
exercise: {a} had {g+1} bags — no wait {g} bags, {k} {t} in each, shares em out to {p} mates. how many each mate get
exercise: {b} says it's just {g} times {k}, so {g*k} each. nah there's {p} kids sharing. how many each really
exercise: {g} boxes, {k} {t} a box, oh and the shop's {x} minutes away, anyway into {p} piles, how many a pile
test: {p} of us gonna share {g} lots of {k} {t}. how many we get each
test: {k} {t} a day for {g+2} days, no sorry, {g} days, then same amount in {p} baskets. how many in a basket
test: {a} thinks it's {g*k*p} each lol. {g} packs of {k}, {p} friends. whats right
exam: It is given that {g} packs of {t}, each containing {k} {t}, are to be distributed equally among {p} recipients. Determine the number of {t} allotted to each recipient.
exam: The aggregate contents of {g.words} boxes, each holding {k} {t}, are apportioned into {p} piles of equal size. Ascertain the number of {t} in each pile.
exam: Whereas {a} possesses {g} bags of {k} {t} apiece and is required to divide the entirety equally among {p} persons, state the share of each person.
exam: Compute the quotient obtained when the total of {g} groups of {k} {t} is divided equally into {p} portions, expressed as the number of {t} per portion.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {g} boxes of {t} with {k} {t} in each. The {t} are shared equally among her {p} grandchildren. How many {t} does each grandchild get?
exercise: The office was "restructured", and {g} boxes of {t}, {k} in each, were left behind. The {p} workers who were let go share them equally. How many {t} does each one get?
test: old man next door popped his clogs, left {g} crates of {t}, {k} a crate, and us {p} kids gotta split 'em. how many each, and quit moaning
